   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "widgets_values": [
    "## MoM unit-sprite pipeline\n\nGenerated by `Scenarios/mom/tools/zimage_graph.py` -- the batch client runs this\nexact graph, so what you see here is what actually executed.\n\n**Measured on this art (2026-09-03/04), do not re-derive:**\n- Two-stage (0.50 then 0.28 after a latent upscale) beats one pass. A single\n  high-denoise pass invents semantics: an ice-lightning streak became a lance.\n- Higher resolution is WORSE. At 1024 Z-Image returns near-identity; at 640 it\n  fully repaints. 512 -> 1.5x is the working ladder.\n- Steps are inert: 8 vs 20 indistinguishable, 2.5x the cost.\n- ControlNet measured FLAT here (sharpness 53.0 -> 52.3 at both 0.5 and 0.85).\n  Switchable, off by default.\n- Downsampling the result with LANCZOS undoes the ESRGAN. Use BOX or NEAREST.\n- The denoiser DARKENS everything (-16.5 mean luminance). Matching the output's\n  histogram back to the source fixes it and is done client-side.\n\n**The VLM captioner proposes, it does not decide.** It is better than hand notes\non legible units but confidently wrong on ambiguous ones.\nAsked about the Air Elemental it answered \"a stylized pixel-art question mark\"\nand listed \"Humanoid figure\" as a NEGATIVE, when the art contains a woman.\n\n**Sampling resolution is sized for the TARGET, not the model.** Measured on\nCRUSADER, single stage, against the geometry-only baseline:\n    192x144  0.14x px  34s  sharpness 0.90\n    256x192  0.25x px  40s  sharpness 1.05   <- default\n    320x240  0.39x px  52s  sharpness 1.09\n    512x384  1.00x px  96s  sharpness 0.98\n512 was the slowest AND among the worst. Pick a resolution the model works at,\ndivide by 16/32/64, multiply by an int to land just above the master size.\n"
   ],
